            <ArticleTitle>A former hockey player with knee and calf pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 37-year-old man presented with severe pain in his left knee and calf. He had no other joint pain, fever, chills, or dysuria. He had previously gone to another hospital, where x-rays of the knees and legs reportedly showed inflammation and arthritis. He had been given oxycodone-acetaminophen, but the pain continued.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
